[
    {
        "content": "<p>My PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/35308\">#35308</a> was about to be merged. But something has changed since I created the branch (~1 month ago), and now, since I updated it, I get weird problems with typeclass inference. Here is a minimal example that shows what goes wrong:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- works, prints Nonneg.instIsScalarTower</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">restrictScalars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- failed to synthesize instance of type class IsScalarTower { c // 0 ≤ c } R E</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">restrictScalars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- works</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Has something recently changed, either about <code>restrictScalars</code>, <code>IsScalarTower</code>, or how positives scalars are treated? In any way, this seems like a not intended consequence.</p>",
        "id": 578740253,
        "sender_full_name": "Martin Winter",
        "timestamp": 1773263191
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Probably <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false in</code> helps?</p>",
        "id": 578740638,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1773263323
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It does. But does this mean I need to set this option globally in the file? There are many places wehre my problem occurs. And again, this is recent. It worked before.</p>",
        "id": 578740938,
        "sender_full_name": "Martin Winter",
        "timestamp": 1773263431
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, there has been a fix to the def-eq algorithm in Lean core which revealed a lot of def-eq abuse in mathlib. For now, until the changes to Lean core have stabilized and until mathlib has adapted the necessary changes, it is perfectly fine to add this option whenever a proof breaks. Please don't set it globally though, this makes it harder to check where exactly the option is needed.</p>",
        "id": 578741579,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1773263685
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you are interested in reading about the details, here is a (long) thread about this: <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113488\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/backward.2EisDefEq.2ErespectTransparency/with/578360835\">#general &gt; backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency</a></p>",
        "id": 578741818,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1773263778
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the quick help</p>",
        "id": 578742713,
        "sender_full_name": "Martin Winter",
        "timestamp": 1773264185
    }
]